{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>And Elohim called the firmament Heaven.</b> HaShem did not want it to be called by the name רָקִיעַ, for this name signifies separation and division, from the language of ״וַיְרַקְּעוּ פַּחֵי הַזָּהָב״ (Exodus 39:3), ״לְרוֹקַע הָאָרֶץ״. For every רָקִיעַ is a screen that separates between two things, and for this reason ״כִּי טוֹב״ was not said on the second day, because through it division was created — for there is no goodness except in a place where unity is found. And therefore on the third day ״כִּי טוֹב״ was said twice — once for the work of the third day and once for the completion of the work of the waters, which possess an aspect of unity, as it says ״יִקָּווּ הַמַּיִם אֶל מָקוֹם אֶחָד״, and on account of this unity He mentioned ״כִּי טוֹב״. But on the second day, from which all change emanates and which is the beginning of all change and division, ״כִּי טוֹב״ was not said. And HaShem did not want it to be called by the name רָקִיעַ, which signifies a separating screen that divides even between brothers; rather it was called by the name שָׁמַיִם, which signifies peace, for שָׁמַיִם is derived from the words אֵשׁ מַיִם — which made peace between them, joined together, and from them heaven was made. And this is what the Sages said (Avot 5:17): ״כָּל מַחֲלֹקֶת שֶׁהִיא לְשֵׁם שָׁמַיִם״ etc. — meaning a dispute whose ultimate purpose is peace, in accordance with the signification of the name שָׁמַיִם, and it is easy to understand. And according to its plain sense, ״כִּי טוֹב״ was not said on the second day because there was no new creation in it, for the רָקִיעַ had already been created on the first day; and the reason for this is that the second day is the beginning of all change and separation, therefore the Holy One, blessed be He, did not wish to imprint the nature of change upon any created being."], :book :genesis, :voice :kli-yakar, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T23:32:52.558302610Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}